## PROBABILITY MODELS

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**▸ STANDARD MODEL**
Based purely on engine evaluation (centipawn advantage). Converts numerical advantage to win/draw/loss probabilities using statistical analysis of millions of grandmaster games.

**▸ HUMAN MODEL**
Adjusts probabilities based on typical human error rates at different rating levels. Lower-rated players have higher draw and loss probabilities even in winning positions.

**▸ TOURNAMENT MODEL**
Factors in time control, remaining time, and tournament situation. Accounts for practical chances when players are low on time or need specific results.

**▸ ENDGAME MODEL**
Specialized algorithm for positions with 7 pieces or fewer. Uses tablebase data for 100% accurate probabilities in simplified endgames.

**▸ OPENING MODEL**
Provides win/draw percentages based on opening database statistics from millions of master games.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

